DESCRIPTION:Cinco de Mayo marks a single day's fighting: on May 5\, 1862\, 
 a Mexican army stopped an elite French force at Puebla\, a city about 80 m
 iles southeast of Mexico City. It is not Mexican Independence Day\, which 
 falls on September 16\, and it is observed far more widely in the United S
 tates than in Mexico. The American holiday was built in California by Mexi
 can Americans within a year of the battle\, and reinvented more than a cen
 tury later by beer companies.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/cinco
 -de-mayo/
